              "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness/skill/review-heatmap",
              "@type": "bootstrap:Skill",
              "ambiguous": false,
              "description": "The review page's heat map: a section-by-metric table that tells a reviewer of a large document where to look first. Says what each column MEANS and what it must NOT be read as, where each number comes from, what a column says when a build lacks its data, and how the colour was chosen. Use when a reviewer or author asks \"where do I start\", reads a number off the heat map, or asks why coverage or QA say \"no data\"; and before adding a column.",
